{
  "name": "Prepare Markdown as ordered Telegram payloads with Apify",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "start",
      "name": "Run manually",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "input",
      "name": "Synthetic Markdown",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        240,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "raw",
        "jsonOutput": "{\"markdown\": \"****\"}",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "prepare",
      "name": "Prepare using Apify",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        480,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.apify.com/v2/acts/creatieve_naald~telegram-message-preparer/run-sync-get-dataset-items?memory=256&timeout=20&maxTotalChargeUsd=0.01",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ {markdown: $json.markdown} }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 35000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": false
    },
    {
      "id": "validate",
      "name": "Validate and expose ordered payloads",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        720,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const rows = $input.all().map(item => item.json);\nif (rows.length !== 1) throw new Error('Expected one result; inspect the existing Apify run before retrying.');\nconst result = rows[0];\nif (result.schema_version !== '1.0' || !Array.isArray(result.messages) || result.messages.length < 1 || result.messages.length > 20 || result.message_count !== result.messages.length) throw new Error('Unexpected result schema.');\nreturn result.messages.map((m, i) => {\n  if (m.index !== i + 1 || typeof m.text !== 'string' || !m.text.trim() || m.text.length > 4096 || !Array.isArray(m.entities)) throw new Error('Invalid message or sequence.');\n  for (const e of m.entities) {\n    if (!Number.isInteger(e.offset) || !Number.isInteger(e.length) || e.offset < 0 || e.length < 1 || e.offset + e.length > m.text.length) throw new Error('Invalid UTF-16 entity bounds.');\n  }\n  return {json: {sequence: m.index, text: m.text, entities: m.entities, warnings: result.warnings || []}};\n});"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "guide",
      "name": "Read before running",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        -700
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Prepare Telegram payloads with Apify\nFor workflow builders who want hosted Markdown conversion without installing a parser. This is our paid Apify Actor; free local parsers and community nodes are alternatives.\n\n1. Import this workflow and configure Header Auth: header name Authorization, value Bearer followed by your Apify token. Store it in credentials, never in this export.\n2. Replace the synthetic Markdown in the input node.\n3. A manual run calls Apify once and validates the result. Each output item contains a sequence number, text and explicit entities. It does not send messages.\n4. Your sender must preserve sequence and use entities without parse_mode. Handle partial delivery and Telegram rate limits in that sender.\n\nApify account required. Current Actor price: $0.01 per successful input bundle; maximum 64 KiB and 20 messages. Check the live pricing before running. The request caps Actor charges at $0.01 and has no automatic retries. A timeout may still leave a completed run: inspect that run before trying again.\n\nOnly supported Markdown is accepted; HTML and images are rejected. No custom nodes or LLM calls are required.\n\nValidated with n8n 2.43.8 CLI import and local HTTP fixtures, including invalid output and HTTP failure. A live Apify-to-n8n run has not been performed. No Telegram delivery is included.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 1020,
        "color": 1
      }
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Run manually": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Synthetic Markdown",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Synthetic Markdown": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Prepare using Apify",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Prepare using Apify": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Validate and expose ordered payloads",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "active": false,
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  }
}
